==[[Range/Lore|The Range's lore assets]]==
===[[Range/Lore/EP7|Episode 7]]===
*{{AC|VoicemailBrimstone64.mp3}} "Brimstone, I met with [[Deadlock]] earlier. It was the first time we spoke about her injuries since those first few days and I, hoping to help, offered again to return her arm to its previous state. After a pause, Deadlock just raised her arm and said, "take this away and everything they gave would have been for nothing". Then she left. My thoughts are so clouded now. I always considered my healing a gift that helped people but, is it always good to undo pain? Are the scars we wear lessons that we learned from, do they make us stronger? Better? I don't know. I don't know."

===[[Range/Lore/EP8|Episode 8]]===
*{{AC|VoicemailBrimstone77.mp3}} "Brimstone, I want to discuss [[Omen]]. It's clear to me that he's on your mind. You seem so distracted in our briefings and... I assume he's the reason you're meeting with [[Cypher]] so often. You're concerned. I am too, especially with the way he left. You know, I've been trying to put myself in his shoes. Finally understanding more about his past and... feeling a sense of shame that he is struggling to overcome. It's a terrible feeling, Brimstone. One that I think I understand because... well I have felt it too. He and I are both burdened by past wrongs, which is why I think I can help. If I know his pain, maybe I can heal it. I'm going to find him, and I'm going to bring him back. I'll be in touch, I promise. Wish me luck."

===[[Range/Lore/EP9|Episode 9]]===
*{{AC|VoicemailBrimstone98.mp3}} "Brimstone, I've been reflecting on our team's well-being lately and I think it would serve us all well if we encouraged the rest to take time away from their responsibilities more often. The trips we've taken in the past have all been wonderful experiences and sometimes I think it's good to remind us all of exactly what we're fighting for. That's about it. I don't want to seem overbearing so please tell me if it seems that way."

===[[Range/Lore/V26|Season 2026]]===
*{{AC|VoicemailBrimstone124.mp3}} "Brimstone, I know the others are talking. I do not blame them, but they need to spend that energy elsewhere. I'm fine! The crystals won't interfere with the work ahead of us and I've already proven that on the field. You have seen what kind of damage Omega can do under their new leadership. This is not the time to rest, fighting back now is the only way forward. We bear the cost until it is done. So do not listen to the others, listen to me. I'm fine! This is not up for discussion!"
*{{AC|VoicemailBrimstone126.mp3}} "Brimstone, I... appreciate your concern but mandatory bed rest?! We are in crisis! The team needs me. They're putting their lives at risk with every mission, we both know it, and if I'm not there to help with-... one moment... I... just need a moment to catch... my... I... I apologize... the crystal growth... it's more painful now. Skye has some solutions but... they don't get at the root cause, I-... shit. Commander, I-... I'm sorry. I'm so... sorry, I thought I was strong enough, I really did, and I want to be. But this is too much, you are right. I need help. And answer your phone next time! I can't believe this is recorded..."
*{{AC|VoicemailBrimstone128.mp3}} "Hi, me again! Uh... thank you for keeping the previous message between us. Not my finest moment. Things are... a little better. Really! The crystals break apart when I rest, so a small victory! It's just... the moment I'm forced to strain my powers again it... comes back. But it's okay, I have Skye! And listen, [[Skye]] and [[Miks]], they're... amazing. I know everyone's fussing over me but the two of them, what they're doing for everyone, uh, for me, without asking for anything in return, I don't have the words to describe it. I just... I need to know that you see them."
*{{AC|VoicemailBrimstone129.mp3}} "Brimstone, I, uh... I have an idea... about how to fix all of this. There's a place where I trained before. [[Viper|Sabine]] knows it. It's much bigger now, nothing like what it was. Back then, I left before finishing my studies, and to be honest... there are some lessons I chose to never learn. Well an old friend runs the program now and... something tells me she'll know how to help. It would mean more time away from base but is that so different from sitting in the medical wing? When we meet I'll tell you more. Then we can decide together."

